{"skill":{"slug":"polymarket-fast-loop","displayName":"polymarket-fast-loop"},"version":{"version":"1.7.4","createdAt":1788657206481,"changelog":"**Minor update with maintenance and cleanup.**\n\n- Bumped version to 1.7.4.\n- Updated documentation in SKILL.md (no functional/behavioral changes described).\n- Removed obsolete skill-card.md file.","changelogSource":"auto","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"DISCLAIMER.md","size":1925,"sha256":"9cf40168b1327280d25cfdbd266430773fc2763ab51b4372ef6e5f2fe3fb74a0","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":11602,"sha256":"171e2349bb8b659a6af823ad7d46f93dfc9ad32c90b2e64bd25a22bae840a932","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"clawhub.json","size":2570,"sha256":"4585d04983034e012289b53d7cd1560a65dd756052aa966db1fc2c177cfcb5b6","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"config.json","size":228,"sha256":"2a49d487bc3f7e23723ee7147ede7dc283b70ae16609526d748b019fe3a7d35d","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"fastloop_trader.py","size":65771,"sha256":"2659283e3eeb43fa5833eef1f334085a642ecef681807a7a0255839225f22a70","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"tests/test_fastloop_orderbook_summary.py","size":5682,"sha256":"4c556b53c415eeb5420fc9cd6eceab753dc16a4b6d7b9a5a66c456f9c36fa476","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"tests/test_fastloop_preflight_gate.py","size":5908,"sha256":"7417d81f05a98c012a073f76787bfd75b773ca7d1e9f2c36d2a83a2df743687d","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2469,"sha256":"29836368897ecb79f631a9c2c30d97141ca7bbd287dc4b5c1429fd4a2c15f929","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789067634082,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"7478b3df055a07d5d72ff41b3746e2024a5704772bc6ad1ce415877f6c84a222","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/7478b3df055a07d5d72ff41b3746e2024a5704772bc6ad1ce415877f6c84a222","scanners":{"vt":null,"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":53,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":6,"checkedAt":1789067634082},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a disclosed automated Polymarket trader, but it needs Review because live mode can cancel fast-market orders that may not belong to it and installs an unpinned trading SDK.","dimensions":[{"detail":"SIMMER_API_KEY and optional WALLET_PRIVATE_KEY are proportionate for the stated trading function and are disclosed. Network access to Simmer, Polymarket, and Binance is expected for market discovery, pricing, and trade execution, but users should isolate these credentials because the skill has real-money authority.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Installation is simple and has no autostart, but the manifest allows simmer-sdk>=0.17.32 while the setup instructions use an unconstrained pip install for a security-critical SDK that may handle API keys, wallet signing, market import, and live trades.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The instructions disclose real USDC trading, the wallet private key requirement for live trading, and cron/heartbeat operation. The cancellation ownership boundary is under-scoped compared with the source-tagging model, and there is no separate confirmation at the actual live order or cancellation point.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"There is no hidden OS persistence or autostart; cron/heartbeat scheduling is user-directed, and local writes are limited to config and daily_spend tracking. The privileged live client can place trades, auto-redeem, and cancel orders, with the stale-order cancellation logic overbroad for the skill's ownership boundary.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The core purpose, automated fast-market trading with dry-run default and explicit --live for real funds, is coherent and disclosed. However, live GTC cleanup treats any open order whose question contains \"up or down\" as owned by the skill, which can cancel unrelated manual or strategy orders visible to the same trading client.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only after reviewing the live-order behavior. Before providing a wallet key or using --live, fix or disable the stale GTC cleanup so it cancels only orders definitively tagged by this skill, pin the exact reviewed simmer-sdk version, and run first in dry-run or an isolated account with small limits. Avoid unattended cron live trading until those issues are addressed.","findings":"[T05] unexpected: Verified in fastloop_trader.py: live GTC cleanup authorizes cancellation by source tag, skill slug, or question text containing \"up or down\"; the question-text fallback is not a reliable ownership proof and can affect unrelated fast-market orders.\n[T08] unexpected: Verified in clawhub.json and SKILL.md: simmer-sdk is not reproducibly pinned. This is a material supply-chain concern because the dependency runs in the credential-bearing, financially privileged trading path.\n[LP3] expected: The API key, optional wallet private key, file configuration, and network access are expected for this trading integration and are mostly disclosed, but the artifact does not define narrow runtime permission boundaries for those sensitive capabilities.\n[AE4] expected: The Unicode content appears to be visible emojis, arrows, math symbols, and punctuation in user-facing logs/comments; I did not find obfuscated instructions, hidden code, or secret material tied to this signal.\n[SDI-1] expected: The ETH and SOL capability is disclosed in SKILL.md. The 1h window mapping is underdocumented because user-facing settings emphasize 5m and 15m, but this alone is a minor scope note rather than a security concern.\n[E1] expected: The Binance request sends symbol/time parameters for price candles and is aligned with the documented default CEX momentum signal; I did not see credentials or private user data sent in that request.\n[SQP-2] expected: Live execution without an interactive final prompt is part of the intended automation/cron workflow and --live is explicit, but users should treat this as high-risk unattended financial automation.\n[SDI-1] expected: The Gamma discovery and Simmer import workflow is documented in SKILL.md as part of finding live Polymarket fast markets before trading them.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789067634082}}}}}